, then by assumption, 
\begin_inset Formula $\exists\ w:A\rightarrow\mathbb{R}$
\end_inset

 such that 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ \{x_{i},x_{j}\}\subseteq A:x_{i}\succsim x_{j}\iff w(x_{i})\geq w(x_{j})$
\end_inset

.
 Now, since 
\begin_inset Formula $w(A)\subseteq\mathbb{R}$
\end_inset

 is a finite set, then it contains a maximum element.
 Let 
\begin_inset Formula $w(\bar{x})$
\end_inset

 be the maximum of the set 
\begin_inset Formula $w(A)$
\end_inset

.
 So, 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ w(x_{i})\in w(A):w(\bar{x})\geq w(x_{i})$
\end_inset

.
 Since 
\begin_inset Formula $w$
\end_inset

 represents 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim$
\end_inset

, then 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ x_{i}\in A:\bar{x}\succsim x_{i}$
\end_inset

.
 Since 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim$
\end_inset

